commit 0bddee9ea3605055af56b72919153092669e6029
Author: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date:   Thu May 21 12:14:17 2026 +0000

    validator+ports: fix REGEX-03 D_MONTH, restore stripped qualifiers
    
    Undoes the constraint-stripping cleverness from the 2026-05 batch on
    three ports. The careful path documented in REGEX-03 (validator-side
    fix instead of per-page stripping) is now applied.
    
    Validator change (scripts/port-weather-validator-core.js):
    - validateMonths() strips parenthetical qualifiers via /\s*\([^)]*\)/
      before splitting the month list. The qualifier text is preserved
      for the renderer (browser displays the original span content
      unchanged); only the validator's parse ignores it.
    - VALID_SPECIAL_VALUES now includes 'Year-round' as a recognized
      standalone value for venues that operate continuously (markets,
      museums, year-round wildlife) — previously any standalone
      Year-round had to be expanded to a 12-month list to pass.
    
    Port restorations (the three qualifiers I had stripped):
    - ports/hobart.html — Salamanca Market 'Year-round (Saturdays)' restored
      (the Saturday-only constraint is the most important planning fact
      for a Hobart port day; a midweek caller finds the market closed).
      MONA also restored from the 12-month list to 'Year-round'.
    - ports/lerwick.html — Up Helly Aa Festival 'Jan (last Tuesday)'
      restored (the festival is a specific Tuesday in January, not the
      whole month). Otter Spotting also restored from the 12-month list
      to 'Year-round (best Oct-Mar)' — the original had this constraint
      too and it got stripped along with the others.
    - ports/la-coruna.html — Seafood 'Year-round (freshest Oct-Mar)'
      restored.
    
    Doc updates:
    - admin/VALIDATOR_REGEX_ISSUES.md — REGEX-03 moved from Open to
      Closed; lists the three pages where qualifiers were restored and
      notes that an audit of the wider 66-port batch is still owed
      (other ports may have had qualifiers stripped that I didn't catch).
    
    All three ports now PASS the weather sub-validator (55 passed, 0
    errors, 1 unrelated SPEC_REG warning each — 'port not in registry',
    which is pre-existing across the batch).
    
    Pattern reference: admin/CAREFUL_NOT_CLEVER_FAILURE_2026_05_21.md §2
    (constraint stripping). Walking the cleanup one port at a time as
    requested — Hobart, Lerwick, La Coruna grouped here because they
    share the validator-fix prerequisite.
    
    https://claude.ai/code/session_017m1iWTcHm8pcJsQFJD2wQV

